th unique title, description, and OG image\",\r\n        \"TypeScript compiles without errors\",\r\n        \"No external database or CMS â€” pure static data in /src/data/blog/posts.ts\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\r\n        \"site/src/data/blog/posts.ts â€” create blog post data array\",\r\n        \"site/src/app/blog/page.tsx â€” blog listing page\",\r\n        \"site/src/app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx â€” individual article page\",\r\n        \"site/src/components/BlogCard.tsx â€” reusable card component\",\r\n        \"Use Tailwind prose classes for article body typography\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"dependencies\": [],\r\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"medium\",\r\n      \"passes\": true\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"US-002\",\r\n      \"title\": \"Write 6 SEO-optimised travel blog articles about JB for backpackers\",\r\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\r\n      \"description\": \"Research backpacker content online and write 6 original, high-quality blog articles targeting tourists visiting Johor Bahru. Articles must be 600-900 words each, written in friendly travel-guide style, and contain keywords backpackers actually search for. Include internal links to /guide, /rooms, and /book pages. Topics: (1) Ultimate JB Food Guide for Backpackers, (2) Singapore to JB Day Trip Guide: How to Cross the Causeway, (3) Top 10 Things to Do in Johor Bahru on a Budget, (4) JB Street Food Hawker Centers You Must Visit, (5) Johor Bahru vs Singapore: Why Savvy Travellers Base Themselves in JB, (6) Hidden Gems in Johor Bahru: Beyond the Usual Tourist Spots. Each article must have a unique slug, proper SEO metadata, and be added to posts.ts.\",\r\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\r\n        \"All 6 articles exist in posts.ts with unique slugs, titles, excerpts, categories, dates, and tags\",\r\n        \"Each article body is 600-900 words of original, rewritten content (not copied)\",\r\n        \"Each article contains 2-3 internal links to /guide, /rooms, or /book\",\r\n        \"Articles cover: food, border crossing, budget activities, hawker centers, JB vs SG comparison, hidden gems\",\r\n        \"All articles have SEO-friendly titles with keywords like 'Johor Bahru', 'JB', 'budget', 'backpacker'\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\r\n        \"site/src/data/blog/posts.ts â€” add all 6 articles\",\r\n        \"Research sources: numbeo.com, hostelworld.com, lonelyplanet.com, timeout.com/kuala-lumpur, thepoortraveler.net\",\r\n        \"Content must be original rewrites, not copy-paste\",\r\n        \"Use categories: 'Food & Drink', 'Travel Tips', 'Things To Do', 'Local Life'\",\r\n        \"Tags should include: johor-bahru, singapore, budget-travel, food, backpacker, malaysia\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"dependencies\": [\r\n        \"US-001\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"large\",\r\n      \"passes\": true\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"US-003\",\r\n      \"title\": \"Add RSS/Atom feed at /feed.xml for the blog\",\r\n      \"priority\": \"medium\",\r\n      \"description\": \"Create a Next.js Route Handler at /app/feed.xml/route.ts that returns a valid RSS 2.0 XML feed from the blog posts data. The feed must include: channel title, link, description, language, and item entries with title, link, description (excerpt), pubDate, category, and guid. Add a <link rel='alternate' type='application/rss+xml'> tag in layout.tsx. Also add the feed URL to robots.ts.\",\r\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\r\n        \"GET /feed.xml returns valid RSS 2.0 XML with Content-Type: application/xml\",\r\n        \"Feed contains all blog posts as <item> entries\",\r\n        \"Each item has title, link, description, pubDate, and guid\",\r\n        \"layout.tsx has <link rel='alternate' type='application/rss+xml' href='/feed.xml'>\",\r\n        \"TypeScript compiles without errors\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\r\n        \"site/src/app/feed.xml/route.ts â€” Route Handler returning XML\",\r\n        \"Import posts from /src/data/blog/posts.ts\",\r\n        \"Use Response with headers {'Content-Type': 'application/xml'}\",\r\n        \"site/src/app/layout.tsx â€” add RSS link in <head>\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"dependencies\": [\r\n        \"US-001\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\r\n      \"passes\": true\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"US-004\",\r\n      \"title\": \"Add JB News & Updates widget on homepage using curated RSS links\",\r\n      \"priority\": \"medium\",\r\n      \"description\": \"Add a 'JB Buzz' section on the homepage between CommunityEvents and the teaser section. This is a static, curated section (no live API calls at runtime to avoid SSR issues). It should show: (1) a list of 4-5 curated news/blog links from real JB/Malaysia sources like Johor Now, Malay Mail, The Star Johor, and Visit Johor â€” shown as stylish news cards with title, source, date, and a short description. (2) An RSS subscribe button linking to /feed.xml. (3) A 'Latest from Our Blog' teaser showing the 3 most recent blog posts. All links open in new tab with rel='noopener noreferrer'.\",\r\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\r\n        \"New 'JB Buzz' section visible on homepage with at least 4 curated external news links\",\r\n        \"Section has 'Latest from Our Blog' showing 3 most recent blog post cards\",\r\n        \"RSS subscribe button links to /feed.xml\",\r\n        \"All external links have rel='noopener noreferrer' and target='_blank'\",\r\n        \"Section looks consistent with existing design (stone/amber color scheme, rounded cards)\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\r\n        \"site/src/components/JBBuzz.tsx â€” new component\",","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
