{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GcRfpiv8WGc91p21BQ2Xkq","type":"tool_result","content":"      \"id\": \"US-173\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement A/B testing with Vercel Feature Flags and Edge Config\",\n      \"priority\": \"medium\",\n      \"description\": \"Set up Vercel Feature Flags using Edge Config to run server-side A/B tests on the /book page hero CTA and room card layouts without client-side flicker or layout shift. Edge Config reads are under 1ms p99 globally, making flags safe to evaluate in Next.js Middleware. Start with a CTA copy test to measure booking conversion impact scientifically.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Vercel Edge Config store created and connected to the project\",\n        \"@vercel/edge-config and @vercel/flags packages installed\",\n        \"A/B flag defined for /book page primary CTA copy (e.g., 'Book Now' vs 'Check Availability' vs 'Get Best Price Direct')\",\n        \"Flag evaluated in Next.js Middleware and variant cookie set before page render — zero layout shift\",\n        \"GA4 custom dimension records which variant each session received for statistical analysis\",\n        \"Vercel Flags UI in dashboard shows flag status, rollout percentage, and per-user override capability\"\n      ],\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\n        \"Install: npm install @vercel/edge-config @vercel/flags\",\n        \"Read flag in middleware.ts: import { get } from '@vercel/edge-config'; const variant = await get('cta-variant')\",\n        \"Pass variant via x-variant response header or cookie to Server Component for conditional rendering\",\n        \"Flags as Code pattern: define flag types in flags.ts, resolve server-side only to prevent client exposure\",\n        \"Reference: https://vercel.com/docs/feature-flags, https://vercel.com/docs/edge-config\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"medium\",\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"model\": \"haiku\",\n      \"_skipped\": true,\n      \"_skipReason\": \"Consistently oversized diff (12854 lines, limit 500)\",\n      \"_scopeCreep\": true,\n      \"last_attempted\": \"2026-04-14T06:46:28Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-174\",\n      \"title\": \"Add complete favicon and Apple Touch Icon set for all platforms\",\n      \"priority\": \"medium\",\n      \"description\": \"Generate and deploy a full icon set covering all modern platforms: Apple Touch Icon (180×180 for iOS home screen), Android maskable icon (512×512 with safe zone), Windows tile icon (270×270), and an SVG favicon for modern browsers. Without a proper Apple Touch Icon, iOS users adding the site to their home screen see a generic screenshot rather than a branded icon, reducing PWA discoverability.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"<link rel='apple-touch-icon' sizes='180x180' href='/apple-touch-icon.png'> present in layout <head>\",\n        \"Web app manifest references icon entries for 192×192 (standard) and 512×512 (maskable purpose) PNG\",\n        \"SVG favicon at /favicon.svg with <link rel='icon' type='image/svg+xml' href='/favicon.svg'>\",\n        \"ICO fallback favicon.ico present in public/ for legacy browser support\",\n        \"Apple Touch Icon has no transparent background (iOS renders white on transparent — use solid background)\",\n        \"Maskable icon has main content within 80% safe area for Android adaptive icon cropping\",\n        \"All icons use the hostel's brand colours and are recognisable at 16×16px\"\n      ],\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\n        \"Generate icon set from a 512×512 source using realfavicongenerator.net or sharp.js\",\n        \"In Next.js App Router: place favicon.ico and apple-touch-icon.png in the app/ directory for auto-detection\",\n        \"Or use Next.js metadata API: export const metadata = { icons: { apple: '/apple-touch-icon.png', icon: [{ url: '/favicon.svg', type: 'image/svg+xml' }] } }\",\n        \"Reference: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Manifest/icons\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\n      \"passes\": true\n[rerun: b2]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1598b8b-caeb-4a6a-b0e7-f4e096d8800b","uuid":"81e273ab-a946-4c74-a338-41e8be292b6d","timestamp":"2026-04-14T06:47:54.378Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"      \"id\": \"US-173\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement A/B testing with Vercel Feature Flags and Edge Config\",\n      \"priority\": \"medium\",\n      \"description\": \"Set up Vercel Feature Flags using Edge Config to run server-side A/B tests on the /book page hero CTA and room card layouts without client-side flicker or layout shift. Edge Config reads are under 1ms p99 globally, making flags safe to evaluate in Next.js Middleware. Start with a CTA copy test to measure booking conversion impact scientifically.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Vercel Edge Config store created and connected to the project\",\n        \"@vercel/edge-config and @vercel/flags packages installed\",\n        \"A/B flag defined for /book page primary CTA copy (e.g., 'Book Now' vs 'Check Availability' vs 'Get Best Price Direct')\",\n        \"Flag evaluated in Next.js Middleware and variant cookie set before page render — zero layout shift\",\n        \"GA4 custom dimension records which variant each session received for statistical analysis\",\n        \"Vercel Flags UI in dashboard shows flag status, rollout percentage, and per-user override capability\"\n      ],\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\n        \"Install: npm install @vercel/edge-config @vercel/flags\",\n        \"Read flag in middleware.ts: import { get } from '@vercel/edge-config'; const variant = await get('cta-variant')\",\n        \"Pass variant via x-variant response header or cookie to Server Component for conditional rendering\",\n        \"Flags as Code pattern: define flag types in flags.ts, resolve server-side only to prevent client exposure\",\n        \"Reference: https://vercel.com/docs/feature-flags, https://vercel.com/docs/edge-config\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"medium\",\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"model\": \"haiku\",\n      \"_skipped\": true,\n      \"_skipReason\": \"Consistently oversized diff (12854 lines, limit 500)\",\n      \"_scopeCreep\": true,\n      \"last_attempted\": \"2026-04-14T06:46:28Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-174\",\n      \"title\": \"Add complete favicon and Apple Touch Icon set for all platforms\",\n      \"priority\": \"medium\",\n      \"description\": \"Generate and deploy a full icon set covering all modern platforms: Apple Touch Icon (180×180 for iOS home screen), Android maskable icon (512×512 with safe zone), Windows tile icon (270×270), and an SVG favicon for modern browsers. Without a proper Apple Touch Icon, iOS users adding the site to their home screen see a generic screenshot rather than a branded icon, reducing PWA discoverability.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"<link rel='apple-touch-icon' sizes='180x180' href='/apple-touch-icon.png'> present in layout <head>\",\n        \"Web app manifest references icon entries for 192×192 (standard) and 512×512 (maskable purpose) PNG\",\n        \"SVG favicon at /favicon.svg with <link rel='icon' type='image/svg+xml' href='/favicon.svg'>\",\n        \"ICO fallback favicon.ico present in public/ for legacy browser support\",\n        \"Apple Touch Icon has no transparent background (iOS renders white on transparent — use solid background)\",\n        \"Maskable icon has main content within 80% safe area for Android adaptive icon cropping\",\n        \"All icons use the hostel's brand colours and are recognisable at 16×16px\"\n      ],\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\n        \"Generate icon set from a 512×512 source using realfavicongenerator.net or sharp.js\",\n        \"In Next.js App Router: place favicon.ico and apple-touch-icon.png in the app/ directory for auto-detection\",\n        \"Or use Next.js metadata API: export const metadata = { icons: { apple: '/apple-touch-icon.png', icon: [{ url: '/favicon.svg', type: 'image/svg+xml' }] } }\",\n        \"Reference: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Manifest/icons\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\n      \"passes\": true","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01RBXWChbTtuVbRn8xnBPQkV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I found US-173. Let me check the full details and understand what needs to be done. The story is about implementing A/B testing with Vercel Feature Flags and Edge Config. The story was marked as skipped due to \"Consistently oversized diff (12854 lines, limit 500)\".\n\nLet me understand the key requirements:\n1. Vercel Edge Config store created and connected\n2. @vercel/edge-config and @vercel/flags packages installed\n3. A/B flag defined for /book page primary CTA copy (e.g., 'Book Now' vs 'Check Availability' vs 'Get Best Price Direct')\n4. Flag evaluated in Next.js Middleware and variant cookie set before page render\n5. GA4 custom dimension records which variant each session received\n6. Vercel Flags UI in dashboard shows flag status, rollout percentage, and per-user override\n\nLet me read progress.txt to understand the codebase context.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1166,"cache_read_input_tokens":64653,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1166},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1598b8b-caeb-4a6a-b0e7-f4e096d8800b","uuid":"d19ef53d-8087-4fbc-a87d-b560c08e5ba9"}
