{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015z7DfrkTaSKn4y7Lzp1BX2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n2\t# Search Engine Verification\n3\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n4\t# Google Search Console — verification token for <meta name=\"google-site-verification\">\n5\t# Get token from: https://search.google.com/search-console → Add Property → HTML tag method\n6\tNEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_VERIFICATION_TOKEN=\n7\t\n8\t# Bing Webmaster Tools — verification token for <meta name=\"msvalidate.01\">\n9\t# Get token from: https://www.bing.com/webmasters/ → Verify ownership → HTML tag method\n10\t# Note: Bing can auto-import verified GSC sites (saves manual verification step)\n11\tNEXT_PUBLIC_BING_VERIFICATION_TOKEN=\n12\t\n13\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n14\t# Sentry Error Monitoring\n15\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n16\t# Get your DSN from: https://sentry.io → Settings → Projects → <project> → Client Keys (DSN)\n17\tNEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://examplePublicKey@o0.ingest.sentry.io/0\n18\t\n19\t# Sentry auth token — used during `next build` to upload source maps.\n20\t# Generate at: https://sentry.io → Settings → Auth Tokens\n21\t# Add this to your CI secrets and Vercel/host environment variables (NOT committed).\n22\tSENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=\n23\t\n24\t# Optional: Override org/project slugs if different from sentry.properties\n25\t# SENTRY_ORG=your-org-slug\n26\t# SENTRY_PROJECT=your-project-slug\n27\t\n28\t# CSP violation reporting endpoint (Sentry Security Issues).\n29\t# Routes browser CSP violations to Sentry for forensic monitoring.\n30\t# Format: https://o<org-id>.ingest.sentry.io/api/<project-id>/security/?sentry_key=<public-key>\n31\t# Find it at: https://sentry.io → Settings → Projects → <project> → Security Headers\n32\t# Leave unset to disable violation reporting (CSP enforcement is unaffected).\n33\tSENTRY_CSP_REPORT_URI=\n34\t\n35\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n36\t# MOTAC Registration\n37\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n38\t# MOTAC tourist accommodation registration number (Malaysian law requirement).\n39\t# Displayed in footer, contact page, and JSON-LD structured data.\n40\tNEXT_PUBLIC_MOTAC_REG_NUMBER=\n41\t\n42\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n43\t# On-demand ISR Revalidation\n44\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n45\t# Shared secret for the /api/revalidate webhook endpoint.\n46\t# Generate a random string: openssl rand -hex 32\n47\t# Send it in the x-revalidate-secret header when calling the endpoint.\n48\tREVALIDATE_SECRET=\n49\t\n50\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n51\t# Stripe FPX Online Banking Payment\n52\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n53\t# Stripe account must be configured for Malaysia (MYR) with FPX payment method enabled.\n54\t# Get keys from: https://dashboard.stripe.com/apikeys\n55\tNEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...\n56\tSTRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...\n57\t\n58\t# Stripe webhook secret for /api/stripe-webhook endpoint.\n59\t# Create webhook at: https://dashboard.stripe.com/webhooks\n60\t# Events to listen for: payment_intent.succeeded, payment_intent.payment_failed\n61\tSTRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...\n62\t\n63\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n64\t# Channel Manager Integration (OTA Sync)\n65\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n66\t# Configure a channel manager (Beds24, Cloudbeds, SiteMinder) for:\n67\t# - Real-time ARI (Availability, Rate, Inventory) sync with OTAs\n68\t# - Webhook handling for booking updates from Booking.com, Agoda, Hostelworld\n69\t# - Prevention of overbookings across all distribution channels\n70\t\n71\t# Provider: \"beds24\" (recommended for small hostels)\n72\tCHANNEL_MANAGER_PROVIDER=beds24\n73\t\n74\t# Beds24 credentials\n75\t# Get from: https://www.beds24.com/ownersarea → API\n76\t# API Key: Account settings → API → API Key\n77\t# Property ID: Your Beds24 property ID (numeric)\n78\tBEDS24_API_KEY=\n79\tBEDS24_PROPERTY_ID=\n80\t\n81\t# Webhook validation secret (shared between website and channel manager)\n82\t# Set same value in your Beds24 webhook configuration\n83\t# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32\n84\tWEBHOOK_SECRET=\n85\t\n86\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n87\t# Vercel Feature Flags (A/B Testing)\n88\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n89\t# For local development, set flag variants directly via environment.\n90\t# In production, flags are read from Vercel Edge Config (configure in Vercel dashboard).\n91\t# Options: book-now, check-availability, best-price-direct\n92\tNEXT_PUBLIC_FLAG_CTA_VARIANT=book-now\n93\t\n94\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n95\t# Local development overrides\n96\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n97\t# Uncomment to proxy Rainbow AI API to local server during dev\n98\t# RAINBOW_API_URL=http://localhost:3002\n99\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1598b8b-caeb-4a6a-b0e7-f4e096d8800b","uuid":"aed3b2ec-e823-40fc-aa85-dc3eaa5cc093","timestamp":"2026-04-14T06:50:13.357Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\.env.local.example","content":"# -------------------------------------------------------\n# Search Engine Verification\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# Google Search Console — verification token for <meta name=\"google-site-verification\">\n# Get token from: https://search.google.com/search-console → Add Property → HTML tag method\nNEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_VERIFICATION_TOKEN=\n\n# Bing Webmaster Tools — verification token for <meta name=\"msvalidate.01\">\n# Get token from: https://www.bing.com/webmasters/ → Verify ownership → HTML tag method\n# Note: Bing can auto-import verified GSC sites (saves manual verification step)\nNEXT_PUBLIC_BING_VERIFICATION_TOKEN=\n\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# Sentry Error Monitoring\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# Get your DSN from: https://sentry.io → Settings → Projects → <project> → Client Keys (DSN)\nNEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://examplePublicKey@o0.ingest.sentry.io/0\n\n# Sentry auth token — used during `next build` to upload source maps.\n# Generate at: https://sentry.io → Settings → Auth Tokens\n# Add this to your CI secrets and Vercel/host environment variables (NOT committed).\nSENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=\n\n# Optional: Override org/project slugs if different from sentry.properties\n# SENTRY_ORG=your-org-slug\n# SENTRY_PROJECT=your-project-slug\n\n# CSP violation reporting endpoint (Sentry Security Issues).\n# Routes browser CSP violations to Sentry for forensic monitoring.\n# Format: https://o<org-id>.ingest.sentry.io/api/<project-id>/security/?sentry_key=<public-key>\n# Find it at: https://sentry.io → Settings → Projects → <project> → Security Headers\n# Leave unset to disable violation reporting (CSP enforcement is unaffected).\nSENTRY_CSP_REPORT_URI=\n\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# MOTAC Registration\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# MOTAC tourist accommodation registration number (Malaysian law requirement).\n# Displayed in footer, contact page, and JSON-LD structured data.\nNEXT_PUBLIC_MOTAC_REG_NUMBER=\n\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# On-demand ISR Revalidation\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# Shared secret for the /api/revalidate webhook endpoint.\n# Generate a random string: openssl rand -hex 32\n# Send it in the x-revalidate-secret header when calling the endpoint.\nREVALIDATE_SECRET=\n\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# Stripe FPX Online Banking Payment\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# Stripe account must be configured for Malaysia (MYR) with FPX payment method enabled.\n# Get keys from: https://dashboard.stripe.com/apikeys\nNEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...\nSTRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...\n\n# Stripe webhook secret for /api/stripe-webhook endpoint.\n# Create webhook at: https://dashboard.stripe.com/webhooks\n# Events to listen for: payment_intent.succeeded, payment_intent.payment_failed\nSTRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...\n\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# Channel Manager Integration (OTA Sync)\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# Configure a channel manager (Beds24, Cloudbeds, SiteMinder) for:\n# - Real-time ARI (Availability, Rate, Inventory) sync with OTAs\n# - Webhook handling for booking updates from Booking.com, Agoda, Hostelworld\n# - Prevention of overbookings across all distribution channels\n\n# Provider: \"beds24\" (recommended for small hostels)\nCHANNEL_MANAGER_PROVIDER=beds24\n\n# Beds24 credentials\n# Get from: https://www.beds24.com/ownersarea → API\n# API Key: Account settings → API → API Key\n# Property ID: Your Beds24 property ID (numeric)\nBEDS24_API_KEY=\nBEDS24_PROPERTY_ID=\n\n# Webhook validation secret (shared between website and channel manager)\n# Set same value in your Beds24 webhook configuration\n# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32\nWEBHOOK_SECRET=\n\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# Vercel Feature Flags (A/B Testing)\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# For local development, set flag variants directly via environment.\n# In production, flags are read from Vercel Edge Config (configure in Vercel dashboard).\n# Options: book-now, check-availability, best-price-direct\nNEXT_PUBLIC_FLAG_CTA_VARIANT=book-now\n\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# Local development overrides\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# Uncomment to proxy Rainbow AI API to local server during dev\n# RAINBOW_API_URL=http://localhost:3002\n","numLines":99,"startLine":1,"totalLines":99}}}
